\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-30-21_US-005.log:22:\\u{1b}[94m[shell]\\u{1b}[0m $ /bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n \\\\\\\"oa://|\\\\\\\\\\\"'$ref|components/(schemas|responses|parameters|requestBodies|headers|...\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-30-21_US-005.log:34:The existing registry already resolves `oa://...` and relative file refs into `targetId`, but it deliberately leaves the raw `$ref` in node content. I’m going to add a pure output rewrite layer that uses those resolved edges plus a kind-to-component-location table, with tests around nested source refs and all component-like kinds.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-30-21_US-005.log:45:I’m going to add a new parser module for output `$ref` rewriting, export it from the parser package, and extend the existing registry tests. The helper will default output names to each target node’s local name while accepting a target-local name map for the later naming-policy story.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-30-21_US-005.log:72:The repo checks are green through full typecheck and schema validation. API-index verification caught documentation drift caused by backticked component section names in a description, so I’m tightening that row to avoid the checker treating them as exported symbols.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-30-21_US-005.log:84:Added output `$ref` rewriting in [`definition-output-refs.ts`](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/packages/parser/src/definition-output-refs.ts), exported the new parser API, and covered schema/response/parameter/requestBody/header/link/callback/securityScheme component locations. The rewrite uses resolved registry `targetId`s, rewrites nested content and refs, supports target-local output names, and preserves registry diagnostics for unresolved refs.\\npackages/parser/src/deref.ts:73:            resolution.target,\\npackages/parser/src/deref.ts:75:            resolution.documentRoot ?? resolution.target,\\npackages/p