IDs and node/ref primitives, with registry graph deliberately deferred to this story. I’m now reading those parser files and the PRD section so the registry fits the existing public API style.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-12-31_US-003.log:93:Added a public parser registry in [definition-registry.ts](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/packages/parser/src/definition-registry.ts) and exported it from [index.ts](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/packages/parser/src/index.ts). It registers unique definition nodes, builds `nodeById`, collects JSON Pointer-aware `$ref` edges from fragment content, normalizes valid `oa://...` canonical refs into `targetId`, and rejects duplicate canonical IDs with source/first-source diagnostics plus optional line/column coordinates.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:43:\\u{1b}[94m[shell]\\u{1b}[0m $ /bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n \\\\\\\"externalSpecPath|nestedExternalSpecPath|collisionSpecPath|\\\\\\\\.yaml#/components/...\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:47:I’m making scoped changes now: a parser baseline file for graph and deref semantics, codegen typegen tests for external alias behavior, and internal docs that record the current path split and known resolver gaps.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:73:Those targeted commands used repo-root paths while Vitest was running from each package directory, so no files matched. I’m rerunning with package-relative paths.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:224:### 2. [ ] codegen: 외부 `$defs` / 비 components schema alias 정책\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:225:배경: 외부 `$ref` type alias는 현재 `#/components/schemas/*` 중심으로 안정화됨.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/e8849d83_2026-04-15_10-32-54_US-001.log:226:작업: `$defs` 또는 다른 schema root를 typegen alias 대상으로 허용할지 결정하고, 허용 시 이름 생성 규칙을 문서화.\\npackages/codegen/src/drizzle/converter.ts:14:import type { TableNaming } from './naming.js'\\npackages/codegen/src/drizzle/converter.ts:53:  naming: TableNaming,\\npackages/codegen/src/drizzle/converter.ts:60:      name: naming.select(table.sqlName),\\npackages/codegen/src/drizzle/converter.ts:68:      name: naming.insert(table.sqlName),\\npackages/codegen/src/drizzle/converter.ts:76:      name: naming.update(table.sqlName),\\npackages/codegen/src/drizzle/converter.ts:92:  naming: TableNaming,\\npackages/codegen/src/drizzle/converter.ts:95:  return convertTableWithFactory(table, types, naming, factory)\\npackages/codegen/src/drizzle/converter.ts:104:  naming: TableNaming,\\npackages/codegen/src/drizzle/converter.ts:107:  return tables.flatMap(t => convertTableWithFactory(t, types, naming, factory))\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-10-57_US-011.log:6:- **Task Title**: Define external $defs alias policy\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-10-57_US-011.log:7:- **Description**: As an OA SDK maintainer, I want a documented policy for external refs outside #/components/schemas/* so that typegen behavior is explicit and predictable.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-10-57_US-011.log:32:\\u{1b}[94m[shell]\\u{1b}[0m $ /bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n \\\\\\\"US-011|external \\\\\\\\\\\"'$defs|defs|non-components|schema root|external refs\\\" tasks...\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-10-57_US-011.log:38:The current typegen scanner only promotes external `#/components/schemas/*` pointers. `$defs` and other external schema roots are currently invisible to alias analysis, so I’m checking whether the existing diagnostics path can make that behavior explicit without overbuilding the follow-on alias story.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-10-57_US-011.log:51:I’m going to implement the policy as support, not rejection: external schema-position refs to `#/$defs/*` and other external schema roots will be promoted to generated aliases using the same resolver-normalized identity and collision behavior as `#/components/schemas/*`. The follow-on story can still tighten broader alias naming collisions, but this locks the core behavior now.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-10-57_US-011.log:52:I’m editing the alias filter narrowly: it will only consider external refs that appear in schema positions, so response/path-item `$ref` objects are not accidentally treated as type aliases.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-10-57_US-011.log:54:The implementation and tests are in place. I’m running the focused codegen test slice now before updating docs, so any naming or traversal issue shows up while the change is still small.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-10-57_US-011.log:92:The final diff is scoped to codegen typegen, tests, and internal docs. I’m adding the required US-011 progress note now, including the reusable pattern about using source schema context rather than target pointer shape alone.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-10-57_US-011.log:101:Policy selected: external YAML/JSON `$ref`s in schema positions are now normalized into generated aliases, not rejected. This includes `#/components/schemas/*`, `#/$defs/*`, and non-components schema roots such as `#/schemas/*` and `#/models/*`.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-10-57_US-011.log:104:- Generalized alias discovery in [generate-types.ts](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/packages/codegen/src/typegen/generate-types.ts:343) to gate on the `$ref` source being schema context instead of requiring target pointers under `#/components/schemas/*`.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-10-57_US-011.log:105:- Added `$defs` and non-components root coverage in [generate-types.test.ts](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/packages/codegen/src/__tests__/typegen/generate-types.test.ts:293).\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-10-57_US-011.log:124:2026-04-15T03:16:42.502589Z ERROR codex_core::tools::router: error=exec_command failed for `/bin/zsh 