{\\npackages/mock-server/src/__tests__/unit/stream.test.ts:87:    expect(generator.fold({ $ref: '#/components/schemas/Foo' })).toBeNull()\\ndocs/references/oas32/10-examples-links.md:19:| <a name=\\\"example-value\\\"></a>value | Any | Embedded literal example. The `value` field and `externalValue` field are mutually exclusive. To represent examples of media types that cannot naturally be represented in JSON or YAML, use a string value to contain the example, escaping where necessary.<br><br>**Deprecated for non-JSON serialization targets:** Use `dataValue` and/or `serializedValue`, which both have unambiguous syntax and semantics, instead. |\\ndocs/references/oas32/10-examples-links.md:40:For data that consists of a single string, and a serialization target such as `text/plain` where the string is guaranteed to be serialized without any further escaping, these fields are also safe to use.\\ndocs/references/oas32/10-examples-links.md:42:For other serialization targets, the ambiguity of the phrase \\\"naturally be represented in JSON or YAML,\\\" as well as past errors in the parameter style examples table, have resulted in inconsistencies in the support and usage of these fields.\\ndocs/references/oas32/10-examples-links.md:43:In practice, this has resulted in the `value` and shorthand `example` fields having implementation-defined behavior for non-JSON targets; OAD authors SHOULD use other fields to ensure interoperability.\\ndocs/references/oas32/10-examples-links.md:180:| <a name=\\\"link-request-body\\\"></a>requestBody | Any \\\\| [{expression}](#runtime-expressions) | A literal value or [{expression}](#runtime-expressions) to use as a request body when calling the target operation. |\\ndocs/references/oas32/10-examples-links.md:182:| <a name=\\\"link-server\\\"></a>server | [Server Object](#server-object) | A server object to be used by the target operation. |\\ndocs/references/oas32/10-examples-links.md:223:              # the target link operationId\\ndocs/references/oas32/10-examples-links.md:245:When a runtime expression fails to evaluate, no parameter value is passed to the target operation.\\ndocs/references/oas32/10-examples-links.md:272:    # returns array of '#/components/schemas/repository'\\ndocs/references/oas32/10-examples-links.md:283:    # returns array of '#/components/schemas/repository'\\npackages/codegen/src/index.ts:4: * Zod 스키마 → OpenAPI 3.2 component YAML 생성 라이브러리.\\npackages/codegen/src/index.ts:7: *   Zod Schema → OasSchema → components.yaml\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-21-08_US-004.log:6:- **Task Title**: Resolve canonical and file refs\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-21-08_US-004.log:7:- **Description**: As a schema author, I want source refs to use canonical identity syntax so that fragments can reference concepts rather than emitted OpenAPI names.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-21-08_US-004.log:25:The progress log shows US-003 already added canonical ID parsing plus registry ref-edge collection, so this story should extend that path rather than introduce a second resolver. I also see unrelated dirty Ralph/session files in the worktree; I’ll leave them alone except for the required progress update.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-21-08_US-004.log:37:The registry code already normalizes `oa://...` into `kind:scope/domain/name` when the grammar is valid, but it currently stays silent for invalid canonical refs, missing targets, and file refs. I’m going to add those diagnostics and reuse the existing ref traversal instead of touching the general OpenAPI resolver.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-21-08_US-004.log:43:\\u{1b}[94m[shell]\\u{1b}[0m $ /bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n \\\\\\\"US-004|canonical refs|file refs|source ref|relative file\\\\\\\" tasks docs packages...\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-21-08_US-004.log:65:I’m adding focused parser tests now: valid canonical normalization, relative file normalizatio