hemas/Log\\\"\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:350:              $ref: \\\"#/components/examples/LogJSONPerLine\\\"\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:353:            $ref: \\\"#/components/schemas/Log\\\"\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:356:              $ref: \\\"#/components/examples/LogJSONPerLine\\\"\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:376:For this example, assume that the generic event schema provided in the [Special Considerations for Server-Sent Events](#special-considerations-for-server-sent-events) section is available at `#/components/schemas/Event`:\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:384:      $ref: \\\"#/components/schemas/Event\\\"\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:543:| <a name=\\\"encoding-allow-reserved\\\"></a>allowReserved | `boolean` | When this is true, parameter values are serialized using reserved expansion, as defined by [RFC6570](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6570#section-3.2.3), which allows [RFC3986's reserved character set](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3986#section-2.2), as well as percent-encoded triples, to pass through unchanged, while still percent-encoding all other disallowed characters (including `%` outside of percent-encoded triples). Applications are still responsible for percent-encoding reserved characters that are not allowed in the target media type; see [URL Percent-Encoding](#url-percent-encoding) for details. The default value is `false`. This field SHALL be ignored if the media type is not `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` or `multipart/form-data`. If a value is explicitly defined, then the value of [`contentType`](#encoding-content-type) (implicit or explicit) SHALL be ignored. |\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:697:              $ref: '#/components/schemas/Address'\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:723:              $ref: '#/components/schemas/Address'\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:799:components:\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:827:                $ref: '#/components/headers/RFC2557NoContentId'\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:829:                $ref: '#/components/headers/RFC2557ContentLocation'\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:834:                $ref: '#/components/headers/RFC2557NoContentId'\\ndocs/references/oas32/08-request-body.md:836:                $ref: '#/components/headers/RFC2557ContentLocation'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:112:Implementations MAY inspect subschemas or possible reference targets of other keywords such as `oneOf` or `$dynamicRef`, but MUST NOT attempt to resolve ambiguities.\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:137:As an example of these processes, given these OpenAPI components:\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:140:components:\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:146:            $ref: \\\"#/components/schemas/FormData\\\"\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:175:* `#/components/requestBodies/Form/content/application~1x-www-form-urlencoded/schema` (initial starting point schema, only `$ref`)\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:176:* `#/components/schemas/FormData` (follow `$ref`, found `properties`)\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:177:* `#/components/schemas/FormData/properties/code` (starting point schema for `code` property)\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:178:* `#/components/schemas/FormData/properties/code/allOf/0` (follow `allOf`, found `type: [string, number]`)\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:179:* `#/components/schemas/FormData/properties/code/allOf/1` (follow `allOf`, found `type: string`)\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:180:* `#/components/schemas/FormData/properties/count` (starting point schema for `count` property, found `type: integer`)\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:181:* `#/components/schemas/FormData/properties/extra` (starting point schema for `extra` property, found `type: object`)\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:349:    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Address'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:371:  $ref: '#/components/schemas/ComplexModel'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:406:components:\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:422:        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorModel'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:436:components:\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:447:        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Cat'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:448:        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Dog'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:486:components:\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:493:          cat: '#/components/schemas/Cat'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:494:          dog: '#/components/schemas/Dog'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:502:        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Cat'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:503:        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Dog'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:542:components:\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:559:        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pet'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:575:        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pet'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:591:components:\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:674:The value of the property named in `propertyName` is used as the name of the associated schema under the [Components Object](#components-object), _unless_ a `mapping` is present for that value.\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:675:The `mapping` entry maps a specific property value to either a different schema component name, or to a schema identified by a URI.\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:676:When using implicit or explicit schema component names, inline `oneOf` or `anyOf` subschemas are not considered.\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:713:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Cat'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:714:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Dog'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:715:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Lizard'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:723:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Cat'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:724:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Dog'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:725:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Lizard'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:746:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Cat'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:747:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Dog'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:748:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Lizard'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:753:      dog: '#/components/schemas/Dog'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:757:Here the discriminating value of `dog` will map to the schema `#/components/schemas/Dog`, rather than the default (implicit) value of `#/components/schemas/dog`. If the discriminating value does not match an implicit or explicit mapping, no schema can be determined and validation SHOULD fail.\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:768:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Cat'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:769:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Dog'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:770:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Lizard'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:771:    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OtherPet'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:788:components:\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:803:        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pet'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:811:        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pet'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:819:        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pet'\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:836:will indicate that the `#/components/schemas/Cat` schema is expected to match. Likewise this payload:\\ndocs/references/oas32/12-schema.md:845:will map to `#/components/schemas/Dog` because the `dog` entry in the `mapping` element maps to `Dog` which is the schema name for `#/components/schemas/Dog`.\\npackages/codegen/src/cli/commands/typegen.ts:42:        typeAliases: externalAnalysis.typeAliases.map(alias => toWorkspaceTypeAlias(resolvedSpecPath, alias)),\\npackages/codegen/src/cli/commands/typ