gets, and file refs. I’m going to add those diagnostics and reuse the existing ref traversal instead of touching the general OpenAPI resolver.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-21-08_US-004.log:43:\\u{1b}[94m[shell]\\u{1b}[0m $ /bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n \\\\\\\"US-004|canonical refs|file refs|source ref|relative file\\\\\\\" tasks docs packages...\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-21-08_US-004.log:65:I’m adding focused parser tests now: valid canonical normalization, relative file normalization, missing target diagnostics, unsupported ref diagnostics, and a transitive nested ref case across registered fragments.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-21-08_US-004.log:100:\\u{1b}[94m[shell]\\u{1b}[0m $ /bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n \\\\\\\"vitest 1665|parser \\\\\\\\| 220|Source ref resolution|canonical/file source ref res...\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-21-08_US-004.log:107:Source ref resolution now runs after unique registry node registration in [definition-registry.ts](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/packages/parser/src/definition-registry.ts:57). Canonical `oa://...` refs normalize to `kind:scope/domain/name`, relative file refs resolve through registered `sourcePath`/`sourcePointer`, and missing or unsupported refs now produce registry diagnostics with source metadata.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/bc493007_2026-04-16_05-21-08_US-004.log:109:Added coverage in [definition-registry.test.ts](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/packages/parser/src/__tests__/definition-registry.test.ts:104) for canonical refs, file refs, missing refs, unsupported refs, and nested/transitive ref resolution. Updated [spec.md](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/docs/internal/spec.md:173), [todo.md](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/docs/internal/todo.md:53), [api-index.md](/Users/junwoobang/workflow/oa-sdk/docs/internal/api-index.md:72), and appended the required US-004 progress entry.\\n.ralph-tui/iterations/44fae87f_2026-04-15_12-29-37_US-013.log:93: